name: a fresh terminal: cursor visible, every other mode off
source: xterm ctlseqs (Patch #411) https://invisible-island.net/xterm/ctlseqs/ctlseqs.txt:917-1185 CSI ? Pm h / CSI ? Pm l (DECSET/DECRST); docs/design/terminal.md, What the VT core handles
size: 80x24
input: a
row 0: |a|
mode: cursor-visible on
mode: cursor-keys-app off
mode: bracketed-paste off
mode: mouse-click off
mode: mouse-drag off
mode: mouse-any off
mode: sgr-mouse off
mode: focus-events off
mode: alt-screen off
---
name: DECSET 1 application cursor keys
source: xterm ctlseqs (Patch #411) https://invisible-island.net/xterm/ctlseqs/ctlseqs.txt:917-1185 CSI ? Pm h / CSI ? Pm l (DECSET/DECRST) (Ps = 1, DECCKM)
size: 80x24
input: \e[?1h
mode: cursor-keys-app on
---
name: DECRST 25 hides the cursor
source: xterm ctlseqs (Patch #411) https://invisible-island.net/xterm/ctlseqs/ctlseqs.txt:917-1185 CSI ? Pm h / CSI ? Pm l (DECSET/DECRST) (Ps = 25, DECTCEM)
size: 80x24
input: \e[?25l
mode: cursor-visible off
---
name: DECSET 25 after DECRST 25 shows it again
source: xterm ctlseqs (Patch #411) https://invisible-island.net/xterm/ctlseqs/ctlseqs.txt:917-1185 CSI ? Pm h / CSI ? Pm l (DECSET/DECRST) (Ps = 25, DECTCEM)
size: 80x24
input: \e[?25l\e[?25h
mode: cursor-visible on
